/* recursive */
int factr(int n) {
int answer;
if(n==1) return(1);

answer = factr(n-1)*n; /* recursive call */
return(answer);
}
/* non-recursive */
int fact(int n) {
int t, answer;
answer = 1;
for(t=1; t<=n; t++)
answer=answer*(t);
return(answer);
}

The nonrecursive version of fact( ) should be clear. It uses a loop that runs from 1 to n and progressively multiplies each number by the moving product. The operation of the recursive factr( ) is a little more complex. When factr( ) is called with an argument of 1, the function returns 1. Otherwise, it returns the product of factr(n−1)*n.

