int func(int i)
{
return i*i;
}

As a practical matter, nearly all C++ compilers still support the "default-to-int" rule for compatibility with older code. However, you should not use this feature for new code because it is no longer allowed. The bool Data Type C++ defines a built-in Boolean type called bool. Objects of type bool can store only the values true or false, which are keywords defined by C++.

