#include <cstdio>
int fgetc(FILE *stream);

The fgetc( ) function returns the next character from the input stream from the current position and increments the file position indicator. The character is read as an unsigned char that is converted to an integer. If the end of the file is reached, fgetc( ) returns EOF. However, since EOF is a valid integer value, when working with binary files you must use feof( ) to check for the end of the file. If fgetc( ) encounters an error, EOF is also returned. If working with binary files, you must use ferror( ) to check for file errors. Related functions are fputc( ), getc( ), putc( ), and fopen( ). fgetpos

