THE STANDARD FUNCTION LIBRARY The fgetpos( ) function stores the current value of the file position indicator in the object pointed to by position. The object pointed to by position must be of type fpos_t. The value stored there is useful only in a subsequent call to fsetpos( ). If an error occurs, fgetpos( ) returns nonzero; otherwise it returns zero. Related functions are fsetpos( ), fseek( ), and ftell( ). fgets

