You can apply the l or h modifer to the n specifier to indicate that the corresponding argument points to a long or short integer, respectively. The # has a special meaning when used with some printf( ) format codes. Preceding a g, G, f, e, or E code with a # ensures that the decimal point will be present, even if there are no decimal digits. If you precede the x or X format code with a #, the hexadecimal number will be printed with a 0x prefix. If you precede the o format with a #, the octal value will be printed with a 0 prefix. The # cannot be applied to any other format specifiers.

