Before any of the variable-length parameters can be accessed, the argument pointer argptr must be initialized through a call to va_start( ). After that, parameters are returned via calls to va_arg( ), with type being the type of the next parameter. Finally, once all the parameters have been read and prior to returning from the function, a call to va_end( ) must be made to ensure that the stack is properly restored. If va_end( ) is not called, a program crash is very likely. A related function is vprintf( ). wcstombs

