#include <cstdlib>
int wctomb(char *out, wchar_t in);

The wctomb( ) converts the wide character in in into its multibyte equivalent and puts the result in the object pointed to by out. The array pointed to by out must be at least MB_CUR_MAX characters long. If successful, wctomb( ) returns the number of bytes contained in the multibyte character. On failure, –1 is returned. If out is null, then wctomb( ) returns nonzero if the multibyte character has statedependent encodings and zero if it does not. Related functions are wcstombs( ) and mbtowc( ). 774

