The seekg( ) function is a member of istream, and the seekp( ) function is a member of ostream. In C++'s I/O system, you perform random access using the seekg( ) and seekp( ) functions. To this end, the C++ I/O system manages two pointers associated with a file. One is the get pointer, which specifies where in the file the next input operation will occur. The other is the put pointer, which specifies where in the file the next output operation will occur.

