The sync_with_stdio( ) function is a member of ios (inherited from ios_base). Calling sync_with_stdio( ) allows the standard C-like I/O system to be safely used concurrently with the C++ class-based I/O system. To turn off stdio synchronization,

pass false to sync_with_stdio( ). The previous setting is returned: true for synchronized;

false for no synchronization. By default, the standard streams are synchronized. This function is reliable only if called prior to any other I/O operations. 807 THE STANDARD C++ CLASS LIBRARY

